60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Candidate D, Wetland Restoration, addresses the drainage and heat issues I found.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate D uses water management, which the habitat fund covers. That helps the budget.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate D is a water feature. The old basin lasted, so this might too.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate D needs water care. We buy that in, but the volunteers can help.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate D manages the drainage. It fits the ground's actual behavior.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, the fund covering water management is a big plus for D.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, yes. But the upkeep is triple. We must be careful with the scale.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shunichi, the drainage data supports D. The other plans ignore the water.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, the volunteer groups can handle the boardwalks and observation points.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the crossing data shows people want firm ground. D has boardwalks.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"Candidate A, Woodland Walk, has high upkeep costs and no fund support for paths.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,Candidate A is all planting. The upkeep ledger says that is expensive.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate A is like the eastern avenue. If aftercare fails, it dies.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,Candidate A needs constant mowing and pruning. The staff are too few.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate A ignores the drainage problem. It will flood in August.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote for D. It solves the drainage and uses the fund correctly.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for D. It is the only one the fund fully supports for capital.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for D. The water feature has a track record of lasting.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for D. The volunteer groups can support the maintenance.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for D. It respects the ground and the people's movement.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
